        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(meeting-bot): avoid stale state during transcript and browser recovery",
        "body": "Related: #109755\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes three deferred meeting-bot reliability issues: transcript cursor polling could replay retained lines under shifted indices after a page gap, untargeted browser recovery could choose a Google sign-in tab before an active meeting tab, and talkback could report ready before microphone state was known.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nTranscript retention now exposes one contiguous cursor segment and drops a disconnected prefix when page-local history advances. Untargeted recovery prefers adapter-normalized meeting URLs over login fallbacks. Browser-managed local and paired-node talkback now require an explicit unmuted observation; unknown microphone state is transiently blocked as browser-unverified, matching the stricter Teams meetings policy. Delayed paired-node bridge recovery pins the session node and forces the existing-session `chrome.launch: false` path, so `reuseExistingTab: false` cannot open a second call tab. The documented externally managed bridge mode remains unchanged.\n\n## User Impact\n\nCursor-polling clients no longer receive old transcript lines again after retention gaps. Meeting recovery chooses a real call over a sign-in fallback when both exist. Bots do not claim speech readiness or start realtime audio while microphone state is unknown.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Added same-epoch and epoch-change transcript gap regressions; 10 focused meeting-bot tests pass.\n- Added login-first untargeted recovery regression; 7 Chrome transport tests pass.\n- Added unknown-microphone runtime plus paired-node muted, unknown, unmuted, externally managed, and post-unmute recovery regressions; 160 Google Meet tests pass. The recovery regression exercises `reuseExistingTab: false` and proves `/tabs/open` occurs only once.\n- Teams sibling proof: 72 tests pass.\n- Fresh post-review autoreview on the final recovery delta: no findings, patch correct at 0.93 confidence.\n- Full changed-surface Testbox gate passed on the preceding paired-node head: format, API and dependency guards, four typecheck lanes, core and extension lint, runtime guards. Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxrjgqsnjs3p2cejvd235ay5`; run https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29600815747. A final-head changed-surface rerun is in progress.\n\n## Maintainer Decision\n\nUnknown microphone state is intentionally fail-closed for browser-managed talkback. It remains a transient `browser-unverified` state until Meet explicitly reports `micMuted: false`; muted, unknown, and manual-action states cannot start realtime audio.\n\nLive signed-in Meet/audio validation was not available in this checkout; the browser-facing contracts are covered by focused integration tests.\n",
